This product includes software developed by the Tategaki Plugin contributors.

The new writing mode (src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/) includes code adapted from Nyoze
(the author's own editor), commit 020b5501, licensed to this project under the
Apache License 2.0 by its author. The adapted files are listed in
src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/ORIGIN.md and carry an "Origin" header. M3a also adapts
the keyboard-navigation modules and the PIS-S3 test/diagnostic approach from
the same fixed commit; its local changes are recorded there. M3b adapts the
range display of Nyoze commit c63cd4a0 (2026-11-04, "PIS-RANGE-DISPLAY1": the
selected-text color by platform and the bands for selected line breaks), which
is later than that fixed commit, on the same terms. M3c adapts the input
surface's pseudo caret from the same fixed commit (pseudoCaretSource.ts,
pseudoCaretGeometry.ts, pseudoCaretOverlay.ts and the input-surface branch of
pseudoCaretController.ts) and the retained-text color of Nyoze commit 38750b33
(2026-11-05, "PIS-RETAINED-TEXT-COLOR1": retainedDisplay.ts, the red ladders
chosen by contrast with the backdrop), also later than that fixed commit, on the
same terms. The armed state of the mark of the last input
(src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/input/recent-input.ts, releasesAllModifiers in
input/composition-intent.ts and the matching part of obsidian/input-surface.ts)
adapts Nyoze commit f25c5d35 (2026-10-29, "PIS-IME-KEYLESS-CONTINUATION1"), also
later than that fixed commit, on the same terms. The dimmed `[label]:` of a
definition line (the inline decoration in src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/pm/decorations.ts and
its rule in obsidian/styles/stylesheet.ts) and the reading that shows such a line
as it is written (source/line-segments.ts) adapt the ideas and the colour rule of
Nyoze commit e1da1a98 (2026-11-05, "MD-ESCAPE-EXPLICIT1":
referenceDefinitionDecorationState.ts, referenceDefinitionLine.ts and the
styles.css rule), also later than that fixed commit, on the same terms; no code
of them is copied (see ORIGIN.md). A prototype in
tests/pm-mode/m13-commonmark-inline.ts adapts Nyoze's emphasis rescue at
commit 0e4e68b3 on the same terms (also listed there).
The classification of what a document action finds on the input surface
(src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/obsidian/document-action.ts, classifyInputSurfaceDocumentAction)
adapts Nyoze commit 58a98a90 (2026-11-06, inputSurface/documentAction.ts, the same
file as at the fixed commit) on the same terms (see ORIGIN.md). The room that the
display reserves for the composing text (src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/pm/composition-widget.ts,
obsidian/composition-presentation.ts, the follow of the surface's start in
obsidian/surface-placement.ts and obsidian/input-surface.ts, the short sideways glyph
shadow in obsidian/short-preedit-shadow.ts and obsidian/preedit-highlight.ts) adapts
Nyoze commit 58a98a90 (inputSurface/compositionPresentation.ts, surfacePlacement.ts,
shortPreeditShadow.ts, preeditHighlight.ts, surfacePreferences.ts, editOwner.ts (the
owner's `insertionCaretAtWrapEnd`, which is the presentation port's `atWrapEnd` in
obsidian/composition-presentation.ts) and the matching parts of inputSurface.ts; the
setting is from Nyoze commit c80df99f, "PIS-S10-PREEDIT-DISPLAY1"), on the same terms
(see ORIGIN.md).

The clipboard handlers of the input surface (src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/obsidian/clipboard.ts,
the beforecopy / beforecut, copy / cut and paste handlers) and the policy of who may
copy and cut from it (src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/input/clipboard-policy.ts) adapt Nyoze commit
58a98a90 (2026-11-06, inputSurface/clipboard.ts and clipboardPolicy.ts) on the same
terms (see ORIGIN.md).

The option C prototype (tests/pm-mode/m13c-inline.ts and m13c-delimiters.ts)
also adapts Nyoze's emphasis rescue at commit 0e4e68b3 (Apache-2.0) and
parts of markdown-it 14.2.0 (delimiter scanning, balance_pairs, emphasis and
strikethrough), under the following MIT license. The production reader introduced in M1-6a
(src/wysiwyg/pm-mode/source/inline-reading.ts, inline-delimiters.ts and
inline-html.ts) includes the same adaptations and also adapts markdown-it
14.2.0 backticks, escape, html_inline and common/html_re. Nyoze's rescue
and fallback at 0e4e68b3 are adapted on the Apache-2.0 terms above.
Local changes and source paths are listed in ORIGIN.md.

